<title>USA: U.S. cotton consumption -- Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton consumption -- Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Census Bureau reports factory consumption of domestic and foreign cotton (bales):</p>
<p>    Jan 97-A   Dec 96-B    Jan 96   Cum 1997   Cum 1996</p>
<p>     812,390    857,423   743,805    812,390 10,329,949</p>
<p>DAILY AVERAGE CONSUMPTION OF ALL COTTON (bales):</p>
<p>    Jan 97-Y   Dec 96-X   Jan 96</p>
<p>	40,891     40,671   37,963</p>
<p>DAILY AVERAGE SPINDLE HOURS OPERATED:</p>
<p>    Jan 97-X  Dec 96-Y   Jan 96</p>
<p>	   144	 151	144</p>
<p>A-0 weeks. B-5 weeks. X-Based on 20 days. Y-25 days.</p>
</text>
